Empty Clip - Top-down shooter RPG
by Alan Witkowski

Home Page:
https://github.com/jazztickets/emptyclip

----- DOWNLOADING -----

Download and extract the latest emptyclip-*-src.tar.gz from https://github.com/jazztickets/emptyclip/releases

OR

Clone the repository:
git clone https://github.com/jazztickets/emptyclip.git --recurse-submodule

----- BUILDING ON LINUX -----

-- Dependencies required --
ninja
cmake 2.8.12+
sdl2
sdl2_image
freetype2
openal
libvorbis
libogg
zlib

-- Installing dependencies on Ubuntu 20.04 --
sudo apt install ninja-build cmake build-essential libsdl2-dev libsdl2-image-dev libopenal-dev libvorbis-dev libfreetype6-dev

-- Installing dependencies on Arch Linux --
sudo pacman -S base-devel ninja cmake sdl2 sdl2_image openal libvorbis libogg freetype2

-- Build executable --
./build.sh

-- Running the game without installing --
cd working && ./emptyclip

-- Installing --
cd build/release
sudo ninja install

-- Uninstall --
cd build/release
cat install_manifest.txt | xargs sudo rm

----- COMMAND-LINE ARGUMENTS -----

Parameters with <> denote required values
Parameters with [] denote optional values

Test a level
-level <map file>

Run game fullscreen
-fullscreen

Run game in a window
-window

Disable audio
-noaudio

Start the mapeditor
-editor [level]

----- HOW TO PLAY -----

Use ESDF to walk around
Use Left-click to shoot your gun
Use Right-click to enter aim mode
Click Mouse button 4 to swing your melee weapon
Hold A to sprint
Hit Space to pick up items, open doors, or activate switches
Hit R to reload your gun
Hit W to switch weapons
Hit Q to use a medkit
Hit C to open your inventory or see character stats
Click Middle mouse button to drop an item
Hit Escape to open the game menu or quit the game in test mode
Hit F1 to open the game menu

Save data is in %APPDATA%/emptyclip for Windows and ~/.local/share/emptyclip for Linux.
